      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{620f7ecc5abcc7434a486858|full_name} We didn't consider it a breaking change because we expected any application to listen to variable change events to also check their value? The initial value even in the script you had originally posted is correctly reported as `false` via OSC, you should always check for `true` instead if you want to detect enabling something.",
